Expected elements: present

Identity bar (exit `← aztec-testnet`, hash, `Succeeded`, `block 63675`, stepping controls, `128 / 345`, phase rail); three prose-only panes each explaining the missing source; `Supply sources`; provenance as a `DATA` row with a `Real Aztec testnet data` badge. No band above the identity bar, no invented source, no fixture content.

No `⊙`/`⊘` glyphs render anywhere — the trace is source-less and the left panes hold prose only, so the recorded glyph question is untestable here.

(a) The fade. Identical ramp in both themes: alpha 1.0 at y1051 to 0 at y1074, stopping 1px above the pane border at y1075 — anchored to the padding box, nothing spent on padding here. But its 24px height matches the 23px line-height, so the boundary line is consumed whole. TRANSACTION pane, `RAW (CHAIN-NATIVE)`, last line `"hydrationRounds": 6,` — 3.85:1 at its topmost glyph row (y1060, sampled against clean block background at x1800), 2.74:1 at x-height, 1.84:1 at baseline, 1.16:1 at descender (y1072). It never meets 4.5:1 at any row, while sitting entirely inside the box. The same line in the dark capture reads 6.17:1 at cap row: light pays 1.6x because the mask composites toward white.

(b) Each badge tone means three things — green (6.49:1) for `Succeeded`, `Real Aztec testnet data`, `Trace ready`; neutral (6.61:1) for `No timestamp published`, `Yes`, `Pending`. The new em dash is #8A8A8A, 3.45:1.

Fixes: floor the mask alpha at ~0.75 in light or clip it to line boxes; split the green tone.

Rating: 6/10

